# What goes into the source distribution beyond the package itself.
#
# setuptools puts the package, `pyproject.toml` and the README in without being
# asked. Everything below is a file a *maintainer* picking up the sdist alone
# would need, and which a consumer never does — the generated stubs are
# committed, so nobody has to regenerate them to use the client.
#
# `tests/test_packaging.py` asserts these are here, because an sdist that
# cannot rebuild its own generated code is a dead end that nothing else
# notices: it installs, it imports, and it is unmaintainable.
include scripts/generate_proto.py
include PROTOCOL-FINDINGS.md

# The `.proto` itself is *not* here, and deliberately: it lives in
# `crates/slate-server/proto` and this package holds no copy. The generator
# reads it from the repository, so a maintainer working from an sdist alone has
# the script and needs the repository for the schema — which is the right
# dependency, since a copy of the `.proto` here could drift from the server's.
#
# Never: the test server is a cargo crate built from the repository, and a
# 100 MB target directory has no business in a Python sdist.
prune testserver
global-exclude __pycache__ *.py[co]
